# Project-check evidence

This directory contains project-owned execution evidence. It is not generated
proof of readiness, permission, approval, security, compliance, or production
safety.

`.agent/project-checks/evidence.json` is a bounded current index written only
by the explicit command below. Prior immutable records move to
date-partitioned `.agent/project-checks/archive/` files; the current index keeps
successor relationships and never rewrites an archive.

```text
python -B .agent/scripts/run_project_checks.py --write-evidence
```

The writer executes only hooks deliberately marked `configured` in
`.agent/project.json`. Commands and version probes are argv arrays and are
passed directly to the operating system without `shell=True`. Hooks marked
`not_applicable` or `not_assessed` are recorded as skipped and never executed.
Routine work may select exact hooks with repeated `--hook` arguments or use
reviewed changed-scope routing with `--changed-scope`. These modes are mutually
exclusive. `--verify-adoption` rejects selective routing and executes the
complete configured boundary.

The writer records the exact argv, observed tool-version output, executable
fingerprint, source revision and fingerprint, Git dirty/untracked/ignored
scope, environment metadata, start/end times, outcome, skipped checks,
declared possible external effects, output hashes, repository mutations, and
limitations. It stores no command output. Repository mutation detection is
after-the-fact evidence and is not sandbox isolation or write prevention.
External effects remain `not_assessed` because repository-local code cannot
prove what an external system did.

The evidence path is excluded only from the project-check subject fingerprint,
so appending evidence does not immediately stale itself. Command configuration
and all other managed project source remain fingerprint-bound. The evidence
store remains inside ordinary manifest and integrity scope.

To run the checks, refresh generated integrity, and then apply the read-only
adoption validator, use:

```text
python -B .agent/scripts/run_project_checks.py \
  --write-evidence --verify-adoption
```

`--verify-adoption` invokes the existing explicit refresh writer after the
evidence append, then invokes `validate.py --check`. It does not convert a
passing result into a readiness or certification claim. A hook that declares
repository writes or possible external effects additionally requires
`--acknowledge-side-effects`; that flag acknowledges execution risk but grants
no authority.
